<!--
  /data-binding — the <data> seam, fetch/iframe, mutation flow.
-->
<div class="doc">
  <p class="eyebrow">Concepts</p>
  <h1>Data binding &amp; live sources</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The <code>&lt;data&gt;</code> seam binds a live source straight into your
    view. You write the data you want; the runtime gives you loading,
    error, and subscribed envelopes — and updates the binding in place.
  </p>

  <p>An envelope is a tagged union: <code>&#123; kind: 'loading' &#125;</code>,
    <code>&#123; kind: 'error', error &#125;</code>, <code>&#123; kind: 'ok', value &#125;</code>.
    The same shape a remote bound to the host's Connect ops returns.</p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.seam}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Consume envelopes</h2>
  <p>Bind the result to a signal, then <code>&#123;#match&#125;</code> on the envelope
    to render the right branch. No manual try/catch — loading and error are
    the framework's job.</p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.match}></sui-codeblock>

  <h2>Mutate</h2>
  <p>Mutations are plain async function calls on the SDK client; the SDK
    pushes the resulting envelope back through the live source. No
    manual re-fetch.</p>
  <sui-codeblock code={code.mutate}></sui-codeblock>

